   (SEFM), Ctr Math \& Informat, ELECTR NETWORK, SEP 14-18, 2020},
Abstract = {This work proposes a method for the development of cyber-physical
   systems starting from a high-level representation of the control
   algorithm, performing a formal analysis of the algorithm, and
   co-simulating the algorithm with the controlled system both at high
   level, abstracting from the target processor, and at low level, i.e.,
   including the emulation of the target processor. The expected advantages
   are a smoother and more controllable development process and greater
   design dependability and accuracy with respect to basic model-driven
   development. As a case study, an automatic transmission control has been
   used to show the applicability of the proposed approach.},
