   APPLICATIONS (ACOMP 2021)},
Year = {2021},
Pages = {150-155},
Note = {15th International Conference on Advanced Computing and Applications
   (ACOMP), ELECTR NETWORK, NOV 24-26, 2021},
Abstract = {The RISC-V compliance test-suites are a set of directed testcases, they
   are used to verify RISC-V processor meets all the requirements under
   RISC-V Instruction Set Architecture (RISC-V ISA) specification or not.
   For processor design, there are many micro-architectures, so the
   compliance test-suites only ensure that the function of the processor
   meets ISA, but not bug free design. Additional, to verify a function of
   a processor, needing a large amount of dedicated testcases with certain
   coverage to highly confirm this function meets implementation
   specification. In this paper, we propose a RISC-V Random Test Generator
   (RISC-V RTG) is used to generate dedicated testcases with custom
   coverage to verify a processor based on integer instructions of RISC-V
   ISA. Our RISC-V RTG doesn't replace the compliance test-suites, but it
   helps improve the quality of verification tasks for many
   micro-architectures in processor design.},
