   2021)},
Series = {International Symposium on Networks-on-Chip},
Year = {2021},
Pages = {75-81},
Note = {15th IEEE/ACM International Symposium on Networks-on-Chip (NOCS), ELECTR
   NETWORK, OCT 14-15, 2021},
Abstract = {Network-on-Chip (NoC) Firewall provides memory protection and process
   isolation. In this paper, we design, implement and validate hierarchical
   Linux security primitives on top of a custom NoC Firewall module
   embedded on the ARM-based Xilinx Zedboard FPGA. Our open-source,
   multi-layer security protocols aim to protect the privacy of application
   keys stored in non-cacheable BRAM. Experimental results derived from
   integrating security within a soft real-time electrocardiogram
   monitoring, analysis, and visualization application allow evaluating the
   software overhead of the proposed security primitives. Preliminary
   results indicate that the performance overhead for supporting data
   privacy is acceptable for one-time authentication schemes. However,
   relative to the processing requirements of the E-Health application,
   security overheads are large, and cannot sustain continuous
   authentication schemes.},
