   High-Frequency Circuits with GaN Chiplets in Silicon Interposers},
Booktitle = {IEEE 71ST ELECTRONIC COMPONENTS AND TECHNOLOGY CONFERENCE (ECTC 2021)},
Series = {Electronic Components and Technology Conference},
Year = {2021},
Pages = {178-184},
Note = {IEEE 71st Electronic Components and Technology Conference (ECTC), ELECTR
   NETWORK, JUN 01-JUL 04, 2021},
Abstract = {The Metal Embedded Chiplet Assembly for Microwave Integrated Circuits
   (MECAMIC) technology utilizes RF GaN transistor chiplets integrated into
   passive interposer wafers using a metal electroplating embedding
   approach. Chiplets in Wafers (CiW) enable high level of integration
   between the transistor chiplets and the packaging circuitry, resulting
   in high RF performance. In this paper, we present the detailed process
   flow, the development of a MECAMIC Process Design Kit (PDK) for mm-wave
   RF Integrated Circuits (ICs), and its application to the design,
   simulation, fabrication and measurements of heterogeneously-integrated
   multi-stage W-band Low Noise Amplifiers (LNAs) using state-of-the-art
   mm-wave GaN transistor chiplets and low-cost silicon interposer
   packaging with 16 dB gain and 4dB noise figure at 77 GHz.},
