Abstract = {Estimating the soft error rate (SER) for processors is imperative to
   adopt a proper hardening technique for increasing the system
   reliability. Aiming to estimate the functional error rates, we propose
   to scale the baseline SER estimated with physical memory sizes by the
   fraction of architecturally correct execution (ACE) bits of memory
   elements (SRAM, caches and registers). We compared the scaled SER with
   the measured SER under neutron irradiation for a multi-core processor
   and confirmed a good consistency.},
