Title = {An Offline Delegatable Cryptocurrency System},
Booktitle = {2021 IEEE INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON BLOCKCHAIN AND CRYPTOCURRENCY
   (ICBC)},
Year = {2021},
Note = {3rd IEEE International Conference on Blockchain and Cryptocurrency (IEEE
   ICBC), ELECTR NETWORK, MAY 03-06, 2021},
Abstract = {Blockchain-based cryptocurrencies, facilitating the convenience of
   payment by providing a decentralized online solution, have not been
   widely adopted so far due to slow confirmation of transactions. Offline
   delegation offers an efficient way to exchange coins. However, in such
   an approach, the coins that have been delegated confront the risk of
   being spent twice since the delegator's behaviour cannot be restricted
   easily on account of the absence of effective supervision. Even if a
   third party can be regarded as a judge between the delegator and
   delegatee to secure transactions, she still faces the threat of being
   compromised or providing misleading assure. Moreover, the approach
   equipped with a third party contradicts the real intention of
   decentralized cryptocurrency systems. In this paper, we propose
   DelegaCoin, an offline delegatable cryptocurrency system to mitigate
   such an issue. We exploit trusted execution environments (TEEs) as
   decentralized ``virtual agents{''} to prevent malicious delegation. In
   DelegaCoin, an owner can delegate his coins through offline-transactions
   without interacting with the blockchain network. A formal model and
   analysis, prototype implementation and further evaluation demonstrate
   that our scheme is provably secure and practically feasible.},
